@KodiakRobotics began our work on the Robotic Combat Vehicle (RCV) program less than a year ago. Even then, the program felt like a major revolution: for the Department of Defense to seek out civilian autonomous technology developers for national defense applications seemed novel, even revolutionary.
Less than a year later, attitudes have truly changed. Nothing demonstrates that shift more dramatically than the House of Representatives’ decision to include language recognizing the importance of dual-use autonomous technology programs in the National Defense Authorization Act, the annual defense budget. Congressional support for programs like RCV will generate new opportunities for companies like Kodiak to leverage our revolutionary technology to help save the lives of servicemembers
